{:edb/db-before-t 1504 :edb/db-after-t 1505 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534817 50 #inst "2026-10-08T07:59:27.081Z" 13194139534817 true] [17592186115100 1020 #edb/ref 17592186312055 13194139534817 true] [17592186115141 1020 #edb/ref 17592186312036 13194139534817 true] [17592186115141 1020 #edb/ref 17592186312050 13194139534817 true] [17592186115142 1020 #edb/ref 17592186312043 13194139534817 true] [17592186115837 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534817 true] [17592186115837 1100 "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0 \\le x < 2π$?\n\n1. $\\csc x = 3\\frac{1}{2}$\n2. $\\csc x = 1\\frac{1}{2}$\n3. $\\csc x = \\frac{1}{5}$" 13194139534817 false] [17592186115837 1100 "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=3$\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=1$\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{5}$" 13194139534817 true] [17592186115837 1145 "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation III has no solutions." 13194139534817 true] [17592186312036 1017 #edb/ref 17592186312037 13194139534817 true] [17592186312036 1089 "q-120554" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312036 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534817 true] [17592186312036 1100 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-\\frac{8}{5}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312036 1113 #uuid "448fe4dd-8417-54f6-89ac-af53b209b5fd" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312036 1145 "Recall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{5}{8}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{5}{8})=(-38.682\\,1…)^{∘}≈-{38.682}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add ${360}^{∘}.$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-{38.682}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={321.318}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSo, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={321.318}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={38.682}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={38.682}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041597/assets/f4ddf01db733d5ee2e73a4b8abb0bec84d9ee2f7be0fea03e99c112456be1c14.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{38.682}^{∘} \\\\  & ={218.682}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=321.318\\cdot 218.682≈70\\,266\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139534817 true] [17592186312037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312038 13194139534817 true] [17592186312037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312039 13194139534817 true] [17592186312037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312040 13194139534817 true] [17592186312037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312041 13194139534817 true] [17592186312037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312042 13194139534817 true] [17592186312037 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534817 true] [17592186312037 1041 "selection" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312037 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312042 13194139534817 true] [17592186312037 1110 #uuid "7f32c989-57c6-5f46-90c7-eeb8eb1f948c" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312038 1034 "62\\,236" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534817 true] [17592186312038 1111 #uuid "6b5d76e6-3f57-520c-8785-6b22b083ccab" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312039 1034 "76\\,234" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312039 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534817 true] [17592186312039 1111 #uuid "f54bacca-4a59-5d5c-9358-4466c0cf8879" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312040 1034 "68\\,547" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312040 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534817 true] [17592186312040 1111 #uuid "9bf6c092-bfd0-5bb0-a388-ac9a40f4f57c" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312041 1034 "65\\,571" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312041 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534817 true] [17592186312041 1111 #uuid "c0a2999a-4447-5293-8d88-3595d69f04ee" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312042 1034 "70\\,266" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312042 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534817 true] [17592186312042 1111 #uuid "b2d441f2-85ae-5973-b984-defdcc4604b0" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312043 1017 #edb/ref 17592186312044 13194139534817 true] [17592186312043 1089 "q-120614" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312043 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534817 true] [17592186312043 1100 "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\n- $5-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$\n- $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=2-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$\n- $5\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-3=-2$" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312043 1113 #uuid "93bbf63d-41f5-5cec-8b52-34cf770cf20e" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312043 1145 "We first simplify the given equations, and get\n\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=1$\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{5}$\n\nNow, recall that the range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equations II and III has no solutions." 13194139534817 true] [17592186312044 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312045 13194139534817 true] [17592186312044 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312046 13194139534817 true] [17592186312044 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312047 13194139534817 true] [17592186312044 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312048 13194139534817 true] [17592186312044 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312049 13194139534817 true] [17592186312044 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534817 true] [17592186312044 1041 "selection" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312044 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312045 13194139534817 true] [17592186312044 1110 #uuid "650f0cd2-1ae8-5b15-afac-110eee214dff" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312045 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312045 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534817 true] [17592186312045 1111 #uuid "874b150b-f17a-513b-a9ac-c5d973fa2e4f" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312046 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312046 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534817 true] [17592186312046 1111 #uuid "8c5e4a7f-b933-5b82-afdc-82404ea473a6" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312047 1034 "I only" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312047 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534817 true] [17592186312047 1111 #uuid "518a85a8-1002-56e5-8b99-69ab87ed0c85" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312048 1034 "III only" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312048 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534817 true] [17592186312048 1111 #uuid "00b14e18-4fdd-5481-ba33-5eaec93fd946" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312049 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312049 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534817 true] [17592186312049 1111 #uuid "f1f881e0-5621-5aaa-8933-de2a3c647820" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312050 1017 #edb/ref 17592186312051 13194139534817 true] [17592186312050 1017 #edb/ref 17592186312053 13194139534817 true] [17592186312050 1089 "q-338723" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312050 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534817 true] [17592186312050 1100 "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation  $4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+3=-2,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$   are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}, $\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534817 true] [17592186312050 1113 #uuid "50e43e47-1126-5fba-b35e-8bf5dbdcd8f3" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312050 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+3 & =-2 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nThen, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{4}{5})≈-0.9273\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=x+2\\pi =-0.9273+2\\pi ≈5.3559\n$$\n\nSo, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=5.3559.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.9273.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.9273.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041597/assets/d8951c588af989cc5a77b213f25a485b8a6e9db1d0f164fc326e65d40c0385c7.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.9273 \\\\  & ≈4.0689\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx≈4.1,\\,x≈5.4.\n$$" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312051 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312052 13194139534817 true] [17592186312051 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534817 true] [17592186312051 1041 "field-1" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312051 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312052 13194139534817 true] [17592186312051 1110 #uuid "9a3d8eea-c858-571b-8fa9-6f400cb4eb0b" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312052 1034 "4.1" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534817 true] [17592186312052 1111 #uuid "6c47ee97-45eb-58ff-9d5d-1c6ccc7b39c7" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312053 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312054 13194139534817 true] [17592186312053 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534817 true] [17592186312053 1041 "field-2" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312053 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312054 13194139534817 true] [17592186312053 1110 #uuid "1f0b6e19-b0e8-5d34-aeb7-260f8ac5dcaf" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312054 1034 "5.4" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312054 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534817 true] [17592186312054 1111 #uuid "4ede57a4-7213-50e1-886b-ce16dd44e947" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312055 1017 #edb/ref 17592186312056 13194139534817 true] [17592186312055 1089 "q-77805" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312055 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534817 true] [17592186312055 1100 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-2$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312055 1113 #uuid "d424b3c0-2159-5871-9aa2-10c0ec4d744e" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312055 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-2 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we have to find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041597/assets/2e1f1ef6c82e30b5f9a591fca432914562f949a7ed5cabc3c4eb92bfecf899ee.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ is not in the required domain $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi .$ To get a solution that is inside the required domain, we subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}-2\\pi =-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3},-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\cdot (-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312057 13194139534817 true] [17592186312056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312058 13194139534817 true] [17592186312056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312059 13194139534817 true] [17592186312056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312060 13194139534817 true] [17592186312056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312061 13194139534817 true] [17592186312056 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534817 true] [17592186312056 1041 "selection" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312056 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312060 13194139534817 true] [17592186312056 1110 #uuid "b7b03399-4e11-5d11-88c2-7fe9c9b164c2" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312057 1034 "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534817 true] [17592186312057 1111 #uuid "5730b548-1b99-514f-b20b-7a8ab001777e" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312058 1034 "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" 13194139534817 true] [17592186312058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534817 true] [17592186312058 1111 #uuid "66f5b60d-4f47-5fbb-9f0b-71d91caf8b14" 1319413